  "skillId": "f.quadratic",
  "kind": "micro-lesson",
  "title": "Solving quadratic equations",
  "minutes": 6,
  "widget": {
    "type": "graph-plot",
    "config": {
      "xRange": [
        -2,
        7
      ],
      "yRange": [
        -6,
        10
      ],
      "functions": [
        {
          "id": "f",
          "expr": "x^2 - 5*x + c"
        }
      ],
      "params": {
        "c": {
          "value": 6,
          "min": -2,
          "max": 10,
          "step": 0.5,
          "label": "c"
        }
      }
    },
    "instructions": "Drag points or sliders where you see them; the description below names every value."
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "The roots of x² − 5x + 6 = 0 are where the parabola crosses the x-axis.",
      "cue": {
        "cue": "highlight",
        "args": {
          "ids": [
            "f"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Factorise: x² − 5x + 6 = (x − 2)(x − 3). A product is zero only when one factor is, so x = 2 or x = 3.",
      "cue": [
        {
          "cue": "marker",
          "args": {
            "x": 2,
            "y": 0,
            "label": "2"
          }
        },
        {
          "cue": "marker",
          "args": {
            "x": 3,
            "y": 0,
            "label": "3"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The discriminant b² − 4ac tells you how many roots there are: here 25 − 24 = 1 > 0, two roots.",
      "cue": {
        "cue": "note",
        "args": {
          "text": "D = b² − 4ac"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Raise c: when D becomes negative the parabola no longer reaches the axis.",
      "cue": {
        "cue": "set-param",
        "args": {
          "name": "c",
          "value": 8
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "alternate": {
    "title": "The quadratic formula",
    "steps": [
      {
        "text": "Any quadratic ax² + bx + c = 0 has x = (−b ± √(b² − 4ac)) ÷ (2a).",
        "cue": {
          "cue": "set-param",
          "args": {
            "name": "c",
            "value": 6
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "For x² − 5x + 6: x = (5 ± 1) ÷ 2, so 3 or 2.",
        "cue": {
          "cue": "marker",
          "args": {
            "x": 3,
            "y": 0,
            "label": "3"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "recap": [
    {
      "text": "Recap: roots are x-intercepts; factorise or use the formula; D = b² − 4ac counts them.",
      "cue": {
        "cue": "highlight",
        "args": {
          "ids": [
            "f"
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "accessibility": {
    "altText": "A parabola whose constant term can be changed with a slider.",
    "nonDragAlternative": "Use the sliders or their arrow keys; the description below the graph gives every value."
  }
}
